/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Constrained ECONOMIC optimisation by hand-rolled SQP (line-search, damped-
  BFGS on the Lagrangian, L1 merit, active-set convex QP -- Nocedal & Wright
  Ch.18 / 16.5).  Maximise economics.NPV by sizing/operating the esterification
  CSTR, up to a reactor-size cap and a capital-budget cap.

  objective:    maximise  economics.NPV   (published by the EconomicsPass; the
                          driver runs the postDict chain so this KPI exists).
  variables:    V_R     (reactor volume,  m^3)
                T_feed  (feed/reactor T,   K)
  constraints:  reactor.V_R    <=  V_max     (physical size head-room -- BINDS)
                economics.FCI  <=  FCI_max   (capital budget -- left SLACK)

  optim09 is optim05's problem solved with `fdMode auto;` (C496, reviewed
  2026-11-25): the finite-difference step of each variable is chosen from the
  response's own noise and curvature instead of one fixed `fdStep`.  The
  response here is the best witness the shipped cases offer: the NPV is
  6.6e8 EUR and carries an absolute noise the engine MEASURES (about 2e-4 EUR,
  3e-13 relative: the solver tolerances of the flash and the sizing chain),
  and the shadow price of the size cap is 2.4e6 EUR/m^3.  An absolute
  stationarity tolerance of 1e-5 asks such a problem for a relative residual
  of 1e-11; the scaled tolerance of fdMode auto (Theory Guide
  sec:sqp-adaptive-fd) and the CERTIFICATE it demands -- the gradient
  re-estimated AT the optimum with its error bar below the tolerance -- are
  what make `CONVERGED` here mean something.  Run the same case with
  `fdMode central;` (optim05) and compare the printed bars.

  At the optimum the SQP prints the active set and the Lagrange multipliers
  (the shadow prices) plus the 5-line KKT certificate.  See the flowsheetDict
  header for how to READ those shadow prices.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

type    optimization;
method  sqp;

variables
(
    {
        path     variables.V_R;
        min      1.0;
        max      30.0;
    }
    {
        path     variables.T_feed;
        min      348.0 K;
        max      352.5 K;        // kept below the ~353 K cliff where the flash boils the bottoms dry
    }
);

objective
{
    kind     kpi;
    path     economics.NPV;
    sense    maximise;
}

constraints
(
    {
        kpi      reactor.V_R;
        atMost   12.0;          // m^3 -- reactor-size cap (shadow price = EUR NPV / m^3); BINDS at the optimum
    }
    {
        kpi      economics.FCI;
        atMost   1.0e6;         // EUR -- capital budget (shadow price = EUR NPV / EUR FCI); left generous -> SLACK
    }
);

options
{
    maxIter   40;
    fdMode    auto;      // the step of each variable from the response's own noise and curvature
}

report
{
    file        optimization_history.csv;
}
